{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1355393-any-more-thoughts-or-comments-about-the-swan-maidens-swan-princes","id":1355393,"title":"Any more thoughts or comments about the Swan Maidens (Swan Princes)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-17T06:54:31-08:00","id":1355393,"title":"Any more thoughts or comments about the Swan Maidens (Swan Princes)?","content":"I really like this kith, but it could use a little refinement. As it stands, it sends a devastating message: that you can't get sexual with someone if you truly love them. There's not even an exception built in for if your character gets married!<br /> <br /> Not that it's strictly relevant, but I'm curious as to whether it was a girl or a guy who created the Swan Maiden kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T19:55:26-08:00","id":1356418,"title":"","content":"I think that's WHY so many people dislike the Kith. It represents some pretty ahh, antiquated ideas about sexuality and purity. Namely, it embodies the idea that sex in any form is always dirty and impure, a necessary evil at best. I'm not sure what it is exactly you want from a swan maiden, so I'm not sure what else I could recommend. Off the cuff you could do something similar by making a Sidhe with like, Metamorphosis? But it's not actually clear to me what it is you LIKE about the Kith. &quot;Sexuality is bad&quot; IS the Kith, so if you don't like that concept (I know I don't), I'm confused as to what it is about the Kith you enjoy. Beyond that, the Kith is a pretty tragic one; you can try to fight it (and if your story teller is playing correctly, you will fail) or you could lean into it I guess? Make a character whose Human nature is a modern person and views sexuality as an expression of romance, while the Kith side is the opposite? And those two natures, you know, DOOM the character? Those are like... the two stories I can see being told with a Swan maiden. Either you're pure and you like that, but die because Tragic Fate, or you're pure and you DONT like it... and die because Tragic Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T03:34:04-08:00","id":1356462,"title":"","content":"I liked the part about giving romantic advice<br /> <br /> Actually, like I posted here a month or two ago, my ST let me create a Swan Maiden who can have sex without penalty as long as she loves the person. I\u2019ve played her in two game sessions so far and I\u2019m really enjoying it. (Technically, you could argue about whether stuff other than actual sex counts, but that hasn\u2019t come up in the game, so it\u2019s a moot point so far.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T09:19:13-08:00","id":1356486,"title":"","content":"All my opinions from last time still apply. If I had to do an extensive rebuild I'd make an &quot;Animal wife&quot; kith that combines aspects of Selkie stuff, but that wouldn't look as much like this kith, that's really the only thing that bothers me after the last thread that Swan Maids don't do the main thing their mythic selves do(put on swan coat shapeshift).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T06:44:16-08:00","id":1362099,"title":"","content":"Yeah maybe they should just have a Shapeshifting lover Kith. Like the Pooka where you can pick which animal Their skin is? Like theirs a shapeshifting Love story about a a girl with a Elephant skin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:02:06-08:00","id":1362110,"title":"","content":"My friend is playing a Selkie and his character is going out with a regular human girl who\u2019s aware of his fae nature. Our ST just bought Isle of the Mighty, so we\u2019re going to be traveling to England and Wales next time we play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T09:23:57-08:00","id":1362134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1355393-any-more-thoughts-or-comments-about-the-swan-maidens-swan-princes?p=1356486#post1356486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All my opinions from last time still apply. If I had to do an extensive rebuild I'd make an &amp;quot;Animal wife&amp;quot; kith that combines aspects of Selkie stuff, but that wouldn't look as much like this kith, that's really the only thing that bothers me after the last thread that Swan Maids don't do the main thing their mythic selves do(put on swan coat shapeshift).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh we have powers for that though if they really want to turn into a swan they can. I see the complaint but We already have a lot of shapeshifting kiths. It\u2019s like why don\u2019t the Claurichan have a shrinking power, they don\u2019t need it they can already hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T11:23:10-08:00","id":1362172,"title":"","content":"Yeah but you shouldn\u2019t have to take level four in Metamorphosis to have a Swan Maiden become a swan. That\u2019s like a Werewolf having a gift to turn into a wolf. Or a vampire having a discipline to drink blood. You kind of expect them to have it as part of the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:09:19-08:00","id":1362392,"title":"","content":"The major problem I have with the Swan Maiden is the <u>THREE</u> frailties that they are saddled with. A changeling of this kith would lead a short, tragic existence, though I suppose that is the point.<br /> <br /> The Swan Maidens/Princes are a neat story to tap into, but I prefer this sort of thing to be the product of a curse (The Magic Swan Geese, The Seven Ravens, The Twelve Wild Ducks, Udea and her Seven Brothers, The Wild Swans, The Twelve Brothers, etc) rather than a kith. And the relational/sex magic of the kith could be a type of musing, revelry or ravaging that any kith could use, though some seem better suited than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:20:54-08:00","id":1362396,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> I agree. That's why I got the ST to change the one Frailty so she doesn't literally have to live like a nun. We've played three sessions so far and my character's Dark Fate hasn't come into play, but then again she hasn't met her True Love either. Can you have more than one True Love in your life or is it literally like a once in a lifetime deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T08:26:24-08:00","id":1362413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1355393-any-more-thoughts-or-comments-about-the-swan-maidens-swan-princes?p=1362396#post1362396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> Can you have more than one True Love in your life or is it literally like a once in a lifetime deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now, THAT is a complicated question.<br /> <br /> True Love in the sense of Storytelling should be a beautiful and terrible thing. And while love and happiness can indeed happen many times, True Love is the kind of thing you never recover from. If lost, at best it should bring a happy ache and at worst terrible pain and hurt. This is especially true for beings touched by the Dreaming. <br /> <br /> In my own life, I have truly loved more than once. Some were great mistakes that hurt more than they brought joy. One seemed glorious and full of so much hoping and wonder that I thought would burst, but turned to hurt so deep that it changed me, in ways both bad and good. However, my wife and I have a different kind of love. It is passionate, loyal, steadfast and true. but it took work. There were the early days of heat, tempered with reality and devotion born of affection and shared determination. And she is my treasure. <br /> <br /> But which of these are True Love? The quick fire that burns and changes you, or the love that is forged and tempered?<br /> <br /> As for me, I prefer the latter.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T08:48:32-08:00","id":1362417,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> I've only had the first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T09:00:37-08:00","id":1362418,"title":"","content":"Swan Maidens, Selkies, Piskies, they all live very specific lives that don\u2019t mesh with every single character concept. You make the character to tell a specific story and that\u2019s the point. It\u2019s not like DND where it\u2019s more permissible that anyone can be anything sure make a Gnome Deathknight warlord sure nothing matters so have fun.<br /> <br /> If you want a more flexible character make a Sidhe or Eshu or something instead. Swan Maidens are tragedy magnets, if you don\u2019t want that then it\u2019s likely the kith isn\u2019t right for the character. If you just want the superficial qualities yeah get a Pooka or Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T09:01:42-08:00","id":1362419,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I wanted a character who was both romantic and tragic. My friend wanted a character who was sort of a player, so he picked a Selkie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:44:33-08:00","id":1362486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1355393-any-more-thoughts-or-comments-about-the-swan-maidens-swan-princes?p=1362392#post1362392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major problem I have with the Swan Maiden is the <u>THREE</u> frailties that they are saddled with. A changeling of this kith would lead a short, tragic existence, though I suppose that is the point.<br /> <br /> The Swan Maidens/Princes are a neat story to tap into, but I prefer this sort of thing to be the product of a curse (The Magic Swan Geese, The Seven Ravens, The Twelve Wild Ducks, Udea and her Seven Brothers, The Wild Swans, The Twelve Brothers, etc) rather than a kith. And the relational/sex magic of the kith could be a type of musing, revelry or ravaging that any kith could use, though some seem better suited than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the whole three frailty thing is kind of absurd. Especially considering how bad the Dark Fate one is.<br /> <br /> If you form a meaningful connection with someone either you or your Object of Affection will suffer horribly unless you instantly break up. And another frailty being you feel Heartbreak especially bad. <br /> <br /> At least give them three birthrights to even it up a little, like being able to turn into a Swan,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 01-21-2020, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:56:35-08:00","id":1362491,"title":"","content":"Dark Fate does pretty much suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T13:35:07-08:00","id":1362504,"title":"","content":"I know, being Doomed to a bad thing those suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T17:18:26-08:00","id":1362553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1355393-any-more-thoughts-or-comments-about-the-swan-maidens-swan-princes?p=1362486#post1362486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the whole three frailty thing is kind of absurd. Especially considering how bad the Dark Fate one is.<br /> <br /> If you form a meaningful connection with someone either you or your Object of Affection will suffer horribly unless you instantly break up. And another frailty being you feel Heartbreak especially bad. <br /> <br /> At least give them three birthrights to even it up a little, like being able to turn into a Swan,</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t mind that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I don\u2019t mind kith not being balanced. Some folks just have the odds stacked against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T21:56:24-08:00","id":1362577,"title":"","content":"Animal wife is a broad myth. Woman takes off animal skin, man steals skin. Man forces woman to be his. While there are other swan shifter stories, there are swan shifter animal bride myths. And they are a fairly common myth throughout the world thus I'd probably remake the whole swan thing as a broad animal wife kith, related to selkies mechanically similar.<br /> <br /> I then might explicitly make a Damsel/Astolfo kith that takes the other bits of swan maid. A kith that's explicitly about being the the true love you fight for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T03:43:33-08:00","id":1362609,"title":"","content":"Animal wife is a broad myth. Woman takes off animal skin, man steals skin. Man forces woman to be his. <br /> <br /> Holy shit that\u2019s fucked up. It\u2019s like kidnapping a Women and taking away her methods of escape,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T07:52:11-08:00","id":1362643,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/239